  data: {
    LLM: "High Card Points (HCP): Ace=4, King=3, Queen=2, Jack=1. A partnership usually needs 25+ HCP to bid a game contract (4♥, 4♠, 3NT, etc.).\n\nFinessing: Win a trick with a lower card by predicting the location of a missing higher card in the opponent's hand. Communication: Use bidding levels to signal your card count and suit distribution to your partner.\n\nDefensive Signaling: Use card play order (e.g., High-Low echo) to signal suit preference or card counts to your partner while defending. Squeezes: Force an opponent into a discard that unguards a master card.",
